{"\003Seven forty-two\004 a.m., Mr. Gasparian: I curse you. I curse your arms so they will wither and die and fall off your body.","Magic Bleeds","Ilona Andrews",false},
},
["07:43"]={
{"It was \003seventeen minutes to eight\004. It seemed to me that should give me plenty of leeway, but I hadn’t been there five minutes before I started to worry that I’d missed him.","The Burglar Who Thought He Was Bogart","Lawrence Block",true},
},
["07:44"]={
{"‘If you’re referring to Sergeant Jennings, sir, when I arrived this morning at \003sixteen minutes to eight\004, he was unshaven and incorrectly dressed, despite still being on duty. I didn’t bawl him out. But I did leave him in no doubt how I felt about his attitude and appearance while serving as a police officer.’","Next in Line","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"She voices her thoughts: “It’s not exactly how you’d choose to go, is it? You’d rather die flying a kite with your grandchildren, or at a great party or something. Not on the \003seven forty-four\004.”","One Moment, One Morning","Sarah Rayner",true},
},
["07:45"]={
{"As for Koch, he spent half an hour at the silversmith’s below, before he went up to the old woman and he left him at exactly a \003quarter to eight\004. Now just consider…","Crime and Punishment","Fyodor Dostoyevsky",true},
{"This morning I took the launch out for forty minutes or so to test the engine. She’s been giving a bit of trouble. That took from \003seven-forty-five\004 until twenty past eight, near enough.","The Lighthouse","P.D. James",true},
{"Tony marks papers until \003quarter to eight\004. Sunlight floods the room, made golden by the yellow leaves outside; a jet flies over; the garbage truck approaches along the street, clanking like a tank.","The Robber Bride","Margaret Atwood",true},
{"\003Seven-forty-five\004 the black boys move down the line of Chronics taping catheters on the ones that will hold still for it. Catheters are second-hand condoms the ends clipped off and rubber-banded to tubes that run down pantlegs to a plastic sack marked DISPOSABLE NOT TO BE RE-USED, which it is my job to wash out at the end of each day.","One Flew Over the Cuckoo’s Nest","Ken Kesey",false},
{"Contrary to his habit of being late, Pierre on that day arrived at the Bergs’ house, not at ten but at \003fifteen minutes to eight\004.","War and Peace","Leo Tolstoy",true},
{"Mr. Green left for work at a \003quarter to eight\004, as he did every morning. He walked down his front steps carrying his empty-looking leatherette briefcase with the noisy silver clasps, opened his car door, and ducked his head to climb into the driver’s seat.","A Crime in the Neighborhood","Suzanne Berne",true},
{"He taught me that if I had to meet someone for an appointment, I must refuse to follow the “stupid human habit” of arbitrarily choosing a time based on fifteen-minute intervals. “Never meet people at \0037:45\004 or 6:30, Jasper, but pick times like 7:12 and 8:03!”","A Fraction of the Whole","Steve Toltz",true},
{"I was doing my exercises and wondering where he could have got to, because it was already \003seven forty-five\004 and he still had not come out.","Wild detectives","Roberto Bolaño",true},
},
["07:46"]={
{"He awoke with a start. The clock on his bedside table said \0037:46 a.m.\004 He cursed, jumped out of bed and dressed. He stuffed his toothbrush and toothpaste in his jacket pocket, and parked outside the station just before 8 a.m. In reception, Ebba beckoned to him.","The Dogs of Riga","Henning Mankell",true},
},
["07:47"]={
{"He looked across at his son. ‘You been booking in all those names, the way I taught you?’\n‘Sure have, Dad. Mr Parnell, \0037:47\004; Mr Parker, 8:09; Mr Tudor-Jones, 8:11; Mr Alexander, 8:23.’","The Grass is Always Greener","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"\0037:47 A.M.\004\nVance had never been more scared in his life. This made a day at a stormy helm seem like a Sunday stroll. The down-draft was spinning him violently now, a lesson that rappelling was not for the faint of heart.","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover",true},
},
["07:48"]={
{"\0037:48 A.M.\004\nVance stared up the mountain, puzzled. The silence baffled him, and then he realized why. He was not hearing the usual high-tension hum of transformers; nothing was operating. They had shut down the power.","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover",true},
},
["07:49"]={
{"\003Eleven minutes to eight\004.\n“You’re always right; there must be a clock in your head.”","The End of the Beginning","Ray Bradbury",true},
{"“When did you next see Dr. Wellesley?”\n“At just \003eleven minutes to eight\004.”\n“Where?”\n“In the surgery.”\n“He came back there?”\n“Yes.”\n“How do you fix that precise time—eleven minutes to eight?”\n“Because he’d arranged to see a patient in Meadow Gate at ten minutes to eight. I glanced at the clock as he came in, saw what time it was, and reminded him of the appointment.”","In the Mayor’s Parlour","J.S. Fletcher",true},
},
["07:50"]={
{"DI Hogan rang the front doorbell at \003ten minutes to eight\004. It was opened a few moments later by someone who was clean-shaven, smartly dressed and clearly expecting him.","Next in Line","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"She and Dakers had said nothing of interest to each other while they had been working and had left the library at the same time and gone into breakfast together. That had been at about \003ten minutes to eight\004.","Shroud for a Nightingale","P.D. James",true},
{"At about \003ten minutes to eight\004, Jim had squared the part of the work he had been doing — the window — so he decided not to start on the door or the skirting until after breakfast.","The Ragged Trousered Philanthropists","Robert Tressell",true},
